          allocated on the stack (i.e., is a local variable or, rarely, a parameter to a function). "Stack  
          Overflow" is often used to mean the same thing as stack-based buffer overflow, however it is also 
          used on occasion to mean stack exhaustion, usually a result from an excessively recursive function
          call. Due to the ambiguity of the term, use of stack overflow to describe either circumstance is  
          discouraged.                                                                                      
                                                                                                            
